{"id": "EUVD-2026-93098", "enisaUuid": "cabfecec-c1e6-33b4-9043-a06ce35cdc8d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix OOB struct field reads in move_smb2_ea_to_cifs()\n\nIn move_smb2_ea_to_cifs(), the while (src_size > 0) loop condition is\ninsufficient. It allows iteration to continue even if the remaining\nsrc_size is too small to contain a complete smb2_ea_info structure.\nConsequently, reads of ea_name_length and ea_value_length can occur\nout-of-bounds.\n\nFix this by ensuring src_size >= sizeof(*src) before attempting to read\nany structure fields. Additionally, reject any next_entry_offset that is\nsmaller than sizeof(*src) or that would advance the pointer beyond the\navailable buffer.\n\nNote that for calls where the server returns a malformed EA list, the\nerror returned to userspace changes from -ENODATA (getxattr) or\n-ERANGE (listxattr) to -EIO. This correctly signals a server protocol\nerror rather than misleadingly indicating \"attribute not present\" or\n\"output buffer too small\".", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:15", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/61812323c037a94e2e7f0db7ee740c34b126bffe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3546cecbf81d98bf3b472d341f981eb48c04f47", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34a3942e787b9c59758115bd65fe1ec89d68c7a4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/13efcd37a9b3d6ffa1579c3dda3e29c893ed9bca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eeb5ef6083e1cefa2ef75041b5597ff228b8d7bb"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98170", "GHSA-qx7m-524h-7684"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01053a30-e63f-3c47-a032-242a90da86ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "075e368e-f637-30b6-b010-b7c15de80ac3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "95907fea4fd8ccc736e0a428e52159b4d42b9958 <13efcd37a9b3d6ffa1579c3dda3e29c893ed9bca"}, {"id": "09db2628-e4d9-30d7-a23c-5829dd823bca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "0a67abdb-0738-380a-97ac-0b4c67d0e2d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1289b0dd-7800-3bc0-81aa-174ec52829da", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.14"}, {"id": "3c001568-b7b7-399e-820f-9cdcbaef9e5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "60eca5dc-3ab4-320a-b922-abfcf3f9a812", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "95907fea4fd8ccc736e0a428e52159b4d42b9958 <eeb5ef6083e1cefa2ef75041b5597ff228b8d7bb"}, {"id": "74df17bc-ecc2-3ff9-ab38-2c05690b3aac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "8743de8e-8b2f-3ffc-9ef8-75f98e1299f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "cd49297c-544c-3750-a235-519913b0a84c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "95907fea4fd8ccc736e0a428e52159b4d42b9958 <34a3942e787b9c59758115bd65fe1ec89d68c7a4"}, {"id": "ec72cfa3-168c-3b53-8202-c088b26691f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "95907fea4fd8ccc736e0a428e52159b4d42b9958 <61812323c037a94e2e7f0db7ee740c34b126bffe"}, {"id": "f5dc44bb-a912-3b87-8adf-9a726572df5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "95907fea4fd8ccc736e0a428e52159b4d42b9958 <d3546cecbf81d98bf3b472d341f981eb48c04f47"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2d566ce3-e683-30d0-a474-8cd2425e09cd", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}